  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4eae8fef-9a27-5aff-8195-c9433d7ca69e" activityNameId="9168e2c3-3a2f-5ec7-9080-a88fcaf17ecc" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, capacitors, 0% water, to hazardous waste incineration</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, capacitors, 0% water, to hazardous waste incineration
Inventoried waste contains 2.52% rubber; 6.59% Plastics from electronic consumer goods; 6.59% Plastics from electronic industrial goods; 7.74% average paper; 76.6% Capacitor (w/o plastics rubber paper); . waste composition (wet, in ppm): upper heating value 6.8 MJ/kg; lower heating value 6.358 MJ/kg; H2O 9785.8; O 151710; H 38272; C 246570; S 248.21; N 2042.4; P 599.86; B 1.3305; Cl 1482.5; Br 724.35; F 34.432; I n.a.; Ag 4846.9; As 1.1463; Ba 32.153; Cd 20.151; Co 3.9391; Cr 8.0335; Cu 21482; Hg 0.12273; Mn 4.0218; Mo 0.72774; Ni 516.94; Pb 239.31; Sb 631.59; Se 0.45766; Sn 1994.6; V 0.098775; Zn 4666.9; Be 0.13684; Sc n.a.; Sr 15.387; Ti 602.93; Tl 0.18221; W n.a.; Si 2035.6; Fe 30928; Ca 675.96; Al 479070; K 118.16; Mg 332.64; Na 89.49; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 12.7%. Net energy produced in HWI: 17.11MJ/kg electric energy and 1.27MJ/kg thermal energy Allocation of energy production: no substitution or expansion. 100% of burden allocated to waste disposal function of HWI. One kg of this waste produces 0.5616 kg of residues, which are landfilled. Additional solidification with 0.2246 kg of cement.;; UUID: 684e7bd7-1493-42d8-a4b8-40e42d0af919
waste-specific air and water emissions from incineration, auxiliary material consumption for flue gas cleaning. Short-term emissions to river water and long-term emissions to ground water from residual material landfill (from solidified fly ashes and scrubber slugde). Process energy demands for HWI.
Location: Specific to the technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Well applicable to modern incineration practices in Europe or North America or Japan.
Technology: Swiss HWI plant in 2000 with wet flue gas scrubber and low-dust SCR DeNOx facility. Gross thermal efficiency 74.4% and gross electric efficiency 10%.
Time period: Transfer coefficients for modern Swiss MSWI. Emission speciation based on early 90ies data.
Production volume: 2 Swiss HWI plants with a total capacity of 53'000 t/a.
Sampling: The 2 Swiss HWI plants, used as the inventory reference technology mix, have a total annual capacity of 53'000 tons of hazardous waste. This corresponds to 39% of the Swiss total installed capacity in 2000. Swiss average plants size is 20'000 t/a. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_684e7bd7-1493-42d8-a4b8-40e42d0af919.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
